# 0108 (M4.T20, round 23) strip the vertex stage from read-write storage-buffer bind-group
# visibility. WebGPU forbids a read-write storage buffer from being VISIBLE to the vertex
# stage (only read-only-storage is allowed there; a WGSL vertex entry point can never write
# to a storage buffer). Blender over-declares every draw-shader resource with a single
# Vertex|Fragment `stages` mask (wgpu_shader.cc:2112), so a fragment-only RW SSBO carried
# Vertex visibility and made the WHOLE BindGroupLayout invalid ("Read-write storage buffer
# binding is used with a visibility that contains ShaderStage::Vertex") -> Invalid
# PipelineLayout -> RenderPipeline -> CommandBuffer, collapsing every workbench/overlay draw
# that shares the group. Live in the visible Playwright rig this class of validation error
# dropped from ~80/frame to ZERO. Fragment-only buffers are not referenced by the vertex
# module (no validation loss); a buffer genuinely read in the vertex stage is
# read-only-storage and untouched. Maps to the census `vertex-stage-rw-storage` deferral
# class. Single-file: wgpu_shader_interface_map.cc.
0108-gpu-webgpu-rw-storage-vertex-visibility.patch
